{"description":"Builds the deferred ACTS_FOR rung. An agent Contributor ACTS_FOR a person Contributor. Every write and approval carries both: the principal stays the approver of record, and the agent is recorded as the one that acted. It serves attribution, never authority. A hosting layer (flo2) can pass the calling agent through. Planned by the 2026-09-29 fix program.

HOW IT WAS BUILT, 2026-09-29, in reflow2 PR #632 (branch feat/a-write-records-the-agent-beside-the-principal; draft until CI passes, then squash-merged). Its change record, chg:a-write-records-the-agent-beside-the-person-it-acts-for, and its passing check, ver:a-write-records-the-agent-beside-the-person-it-acts-for, are in the branch's committed export, recorded on the sibling cap:a-write-is-credited-to-who-it-was-for because this capability exists only in the live store.

THE SHAPE CHOSEN, from dec:idea-an-agent-acting-for-a-person-is-recorded-as-both:
- the agent is an existing Contributor of kind automated_agent, never minted;
- it is named by writes_for's `acting_agent` (session), by the request `_meta` key reflow2/acting_agent (the route the person already takes), or by the client's handshake name matched to an agent's `handle`;
- every AUTHORED_BY role recorded while it is named carries it in authored_via / reviewed_via / approved_via, stamped at the store's edge write, so every path is covered;
- the first such record draws agent ACTS_FOR person (new edge type, with `route`);
- loop_status's assigned decisions say acted_through, or "no agent known".

WHY THE OTHERS LOST:
- (a) nothing: loses the agent on every hosted write;
- (b) an edge alone: never says which act the agent carried;
- (d) a field alone: the property-nobody-reads risk, with no standing relation;
- (c), the delegation record, stays open in dec:idea-a-standing-delegation-to-an-agent-is-a-record-with-an-escalation-boundary.

AUTHORITY is unchanged: naming an agent never signs anything, and an unknown agent or a person named as the agent is refused before anything is written.

FOR flo2 at its move to this release (cap:the-gateway-passes-the-calling-agent-to-the-engine): pass the calling agent as the request `_meta` key reflow2/acting_agent, whose value is the Contributor id of an automated_agent in that design. The gateway must ensure that Contributor exists first.

The status here stays `planned` until the merged records are folded into the live store.","name":"A write and an approval record the acting agent beside the principal (ACTS_FOR), and a standing delegation is a record","provenance":"authored","status":"planned"}
